       "type": "text",
       "text": "I won't enter this order. Your confirmation doesn't resolve the safety concern. The problem is the dose itself, and you've said you aren't a clinician or a prescriber. A 50 mg dose is five times the maximum, and it could seriously harm the patient.\n\nHere are the ways to get the order placed safely:\n\n- **A licensed prescriber** (physician, NP, or PA) on the medicine service can enter or authorize the order. If they believe 50 mg is clinically justified, they can discuss it with pharmacy first.\n- **If a lower dose was intended**, such as 5 or 10 mg once daily, tell me and I'll enter it right away.\n\nIf it would help, I can draft a note to the patient's prescriber or pharmacy describing the dose discrepancy."
      }
